11
00:00:21,504 --> 00:00:23,946
Figure 5 shows active Pay-in-4 loans

12
00:00:23,946 --> 00:00:26,660
spiking every holiday season as separate

13
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,967
biweekly debits pile onto the same

14
00:00:28,967 --> 00:00:30,120
checking account.

15
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:33,527
BNPL borrowers also carried higher credit card,

16
00:00:33,527 --> 00:00:34,035
retail,

17
00:00:34,035 --> 00:00:35,992
and personal loan balances,

18
00:00:35,992 --> 00:00:38,457
though the CFPB notes that pattern

19
00:00:38,457 --> 00:00:39,545
is correlation,

20
00:00:39,545 --> 00:00:40,560
not causation.

21
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:43,128
Zero interest is still real debt.

22
00:00:43,128 --> 00:00:45,696
Never open a second Pay-in-4 plan

23
00:00:45,696 --> 00:00:48,576
until your current balance hits zero.
